# App Architecture

**Architecture:** Full-stack Next.js 15 App Router with Server Actions.

## Directory Structure

```
app/
├── _features/          # Domain modules (business logic)
├── _lib/               # Shared infrastructure
├── (product)/          # Authenticated product routes (HQ, People, Plays, Spaces)
├── (settings)/         # Full-page settings routes
├── (public)/           # Marketing (no auth)
├── (sandbox)/          # Dev-login only
├── api/                # Webhooks only
└── actions/            # Cross-feature actions
```

## Key Patterns

### Feature-First Organization
```typescript
// GOOD - Feature module
import { updatePerson } from '@/app/_features/people/actions'

// AVOID - Route-embedded
import { createProject } from './actions'
```

### Server Actions for Mutations
```typescript
"use server"
import { revalidatePath } from 'next/cache'

export async function createProject(data: ProjectInput) {
  const supabase = await createServerClient()
  // ... mutation logic
  revalidatePath('/hq')
}
```

## Canonical Routes

Use `/hq`, `/people`, `/spaces`, `/sources`, `/plays`, `/memory` — not `/studio`, `/clients`, `/bridge`, `/table`, or `/connections` for new work.

Connectors and the capture stream live at `/sources` (tabs: Connectors / Activity — `?tab=stream` is a legacy alias). Plays is slimmed to Queue / Playbooks / Activity; Memory has Map / Activity / Rules tabs.

Legacy paths redirect in `middleware.ts` and `app/_features/plays/plays-tab-routing.ts`. See `docs/architecture/legacy-naming.md`. Learn-layer memory enrichment is Memory Care (`app/_features/memory/care/`), not playbooks — see `docs/architecture/memory-care.md`.
